Distributed Student Management System:

A professional Java-based enterprise application featuring 
a decoupled Client-Server architecture,
secure authentication, and a multi-format reporting engine.

🚀 Core FeaturesDistributed Architecture:

Decoupled Client/Server communication using Java RMI.
Secure Authentication: User registration and login secured by BCrypt password hashing.

OTP Verification: 
Integrated Apache ActiveMQ for asynchronous
One-Time Password delivery during registration and password recovery.

Advanced Reporting:
Export system data directly to PDF, XLSX, and CSV using iText and Apache POI.

Persistence Layer: 
Robust Data Access Objects (DAO) using Hibernate ORM and PostgreSQL.
Email Integration: Automated system notifications using JavaMail API.

🛠️ Technology Stack Layer Technologies Used FrontendJava Swing, FlatLaf (UI), 
NetBeans IDEMiddlewareJava RMI (Remote Method Invocation),
ActiveMQBackendJava 8 (JDK 1.8), 
Hibernate 4.3.xDatabase PostgreSQL 
LibrariesiText 5 (PDF), Apache POI (Excel), BCrypt (Security)
🏗️ Architecture & LogicThe system is divided into two main components:

1. The Server (StudentServer)Acts as the central "Brain." 
It manages the Hibernate Session Factory, hosts the RMI Registry, 
and interacts with the ActiveMQ Broker to queue OTP messages.
It ensures that the database is never exposed directly to the user.

2. The Client (StudentClient)A desktop application that provides
a modern dashboard for managing Departments, Courses, and Students. 
It consumes the RMI services and includes a specialized ReportExporter 
utility that transforms Java Object Lists into physical documents.

